WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.375
The rule is simple: one front door.

2
00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:05.800
Nothing is handled as ad
hoc email to the cloud team.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.214
The team mailbox gets a mail-flow rule that
redirects into the ticketing platform,

4
00:00:11.214 --> 00:00:16.150
and the detail matters: a blind copy
leaves two queues, a redirect leaves one.

5
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:20.275
Run the rule in audit mode
first, compare, then enforce.

6
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:25.393
New mail becomes a triage record with nobody
assigned, and a reroute rule pulls back

7
00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:30.363
anything sent straight to cloud services,
because old habits survive a redirect.

8
00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:34.501
Cloud services is the escalation
tier, not a second inbox.

9
00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:39.287
Approvals carry due dates that reject,
so silence never grants access.

10
00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:42.910
Once a request is in, triage
decides where it goes.
